  "Core Rules EM-4 record table (line 133) / EM-21 subject table (line 239) / EM-23 W0 (line 249) / EM-28 post_restore / EM-30 / Edge Cases (line 814): [main review; creative-director spot-check confirmed] `body_id` is canonical (C) for every static emitter (FIXTURE, NODE_LANTERN, DEPLOYABLE, FAULT_GLOW) and for OBJECT, ITEM and HORROR subjects. It is set once from Layout `body_of(section_id)`. EM-23 W0 rewrites only the BEAM's and the ACTOR's `body_id` (line 249). Layout LM2 `attach_section` (ship-section-and-layout-data-model.md lines 273 and 309) re-bases the absorbed body's sections onto the host body and marks the absorbed body DISSOLVED. EM-5 and the Interactions row (line 361) say weld and cut call no Emitter mutator, and E1 runs only at `init_world`. After the MVP weld ('home+B welded', S3/S4), the player's beam and ACTOR therefore carry the home body id, while B's fixtures, lanterns, sticks, fault glows and objects keep B's dissolved id. EM-18/EM-30 then give 0 contribution: the player's beam lights none of B's objects, and B's own lights stop counting toward the player. The Edge Case at line 814 only considers a detached section, so the welded case is not handled anywhere. This makes the sim disagree with what is drawn on the core boarding loop, which breaks Pillar 1 directly. It is not a rethink: one field's derivation rule is wrong."
